  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rapid Response to mitigate the negative impact of drought in Southwest, Galmudug, Hirshabelle, Jubaland states, and Banadir region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this $3 million WHO project is to reduce drought-related morbidity and mortality in high-risk districts. To that end, WHO will scale up access to primary healthcare consultative services, provide treatment for the most common causes of morbidity and mortality, including child malnutrition, deploy district-level rapid response teams to strengthen timely detection, investigation and validation of health events, and implement health promotion campaigns, among other life-saving activities. In total, WHO will reach 244,531 people, including 72,137 women, 96,590 children and 19,562 people with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
